WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 10.2 · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
Working out which policies you actually need

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
A new initiative needs fewer policies than you think: choose them from what you will do.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.281
A policy states a principle or rule; a procedure explains how people apply it. A new initiative needs fewer policies than you might think, chosen from what you will actually do.

4
00:00:26.681 --> 00:00:27.281
Three priority groups

5
00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:38.981
Before you start: A legal duty or a high risk from your very first activity. For example: Safeguarding, food hygiene and consent forms before the first trainee starts, since some are 17.

6
00:00:38.981 --> 00:00:49.941
Required soon: Triggered by registration, the first hire, growth or a new activity. For example: Full HR policies before the bakery hires its first baker for the year-two shop.

7
00:00:49.941 --> 00:01:01.359
Good practice: Useful, but not yet required by law or by your main risks. For example: A food-waste policy for the bakery, planned for its second year.

8
00:01:01.759 --> 00:01:02.359
Why fewer is better

9
00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:07.663
1. Copied policies that nobody follows create risks of their own.

10
00:01:07.663 --> 00:01:12.226
2. Focusing on the essentials saves your limited time.

11
00:01:12.226 --> 00:01:18.159
3. Funders and partners can see you know what matters.

12
00:01:18.559 --> 00:01:19.159
What it shapes

13
00:01:19.159 --> 00:01:24.833
1. Your policy register: owner, approval route and review date for each.

14
00:01:24.833 --> 00:01:30.137
2. The core, safeguarding, data and HR policies in this module.

15
00:01:30.137 --> 00:01:36.070
3. Where you need qualified local advice before you launch.

16
00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:37.070
What to avoid

17
00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:42.004
Copying a thick folder of policies from another organisation.

18
00:01:42.004 --> 00:01:47.307
Writing policies without procedures that show how to apply them.

19
00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:53.241
Forgetting what funders and customers will require by contract.

20
00:01:53.841 --> 00:01:55.641
You build a prioritised policy register for your launch and first year.

21
00:01:55.641 --> 00:01:59.641
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:01.141 --> 00:02:04.241
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
